## Endpoints

### Data Read (12)
- `GET /{id}` — Retrieve data for a specific ID.
- `GET /programs/{programId}` — Retrieve information about a program.
- `GET /programs/keycloak-bug-bounty-program/report-templates` — Get report templates for a program.
- `GET /programs/keycloak-bug-bounty-program/reports/draft` — Get draft reports for a program.
- `GET /types/{typeId}` — Get details for a specific type.
- `GET /types/bug/category` — Get bug category types.
- `GET /user-guide/general` — Get general user guide information.
- `GET /user/{userId}` — Get details for a specific user.
- `GET /user/notifications/unread` — Retrieve unread notifications for the user.
- `GET /utils/countries` — Fetch a list of countries.
- `GET /v2/hunter/access/programs` — Get programs the hunter has access to.
- `GET /v2/manager/access/business-units` — Get business units the manager has access to.

### Data Write (1)
- `POST /v2/hunter/reports` — Submit a new report.

### Config (3)
- `GET /assets/data/app-config.json` — Fetch application configuration.
- `GET /settings/env` — Retrieve environment settings.
- `GET /user/preferences/settings` — Get user preference settings.

## Quick Start

### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow
- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).
- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.
- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode="backend"`.

Example:
```text
unbrowse_replay { service: "yeswehack", executionMode: "backend", endpoint: "GET /{id}" }
```

Here are a few examples to get you started with the YesWeHack API:

```typescript
// Retrieve program information for a specific program ID.
async function getProgramDetails(programId: string) {
  try {
    const program = await client.programs({ programId });
    console.log(`Program Name: ${program.name}`);
    return program;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Failed to retrieve program details:", error);
    return null;
  }
}
```

```typescript
